---
name: Global Security
description: Security boundaries, credential handling, secrets, pre-deploy gates. All agents enforce always.
alwaysApply: true
---

## Absolute Prohibitions

- ❌ Never commit secrets — `.env*`, `appsettings.Development.json`, API keys, JWT secrets, connection strings
- ❌ Never run `--no-verify`, `--force-push` to main, or skip architecture tests
- ❌ Never delete RBAC entries without removing corresponding endpoints
- ❌ Never return sensitive data (password hashes, tokens, internal IDs) in Output DTOs
- ❌ Never log sensitive fields — mask PII, credentials, tokens in Serilog destructuring

## Credential Exposure Procedure

If a credential is found in code:
1. Stop immediately — do not commit, do not push
2. Alert user: file + line + secret type
3. Suggest: `git filter-repo --path <file> --invert-paths` to purge history
4. Rotate credential before continuing any work

## Pre-Deploy Checklist (mandatory before merging to main)

- [ ] `trivy image --exit-code 1 --severity HIGH,CRITICAL <image>` passes
- [ ] `git diff` reviewed — no secrets or credentials in changeset
- [ ] JWT secret ≥32 characters configured in environment (never `appsettings.json`)
- [ ] `docs/security/RBAC_MATRIX.md` updated if endpoints were added or removed
- [ ] `dotnet test tests/ArchitectureTests` passes
- [ ] `dotnet list package --vulnerable` — no HIGH/CRITICAL packages
- [ ] All protected endpoints use `[Authorize(Policy = "...")]` — never bare `[Authorize]`
- [ ] No `AllowAnonymous` added without explicit user confirmation

## Secrets Management Rules

- Use `dotnet user-secrets` for local dev — never hardcode in any config file
- Production secrets: environment variables or Azure Key Vault / AWS Secrets Manager
- Password hashing: PBKDF2 (via `IPasswordHasher<T>`) — never MD5, SHA1, plain bcrypt without cost
- Request logging must mask: `Password`, `Token`, `Secret`, `Key`, `Authorization`, `CreditCard`

## Tenant Isolation

- Every query against a multi-tenant table must filter by `TenantId` — enforced by `MultiTenantSaveChangesInterceptor`
- Never bypass tenant filter with `.IgnoreQueryFilters()` without explicit user confirmation and documented justification
